WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.130
- Did you like doing choir?

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.380
- Yeah, so choir, I went
to a Christian girls school

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.213
- Yeah.
- for high school--

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:06.410
- Oh, only girls.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.464
- Yeah, only girls.

00:00:07.464 --> 00:00:08.297
- Interesting.

00:00:08.297 --> 00:00:10.210
- And we had a choir
that was called 12 voice.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.370
It wasn't a very unique name

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.230
'cause they were just 12 people in it.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.540
You got selected

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.830
and we'd basically, we
had gigs though, Kelly.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.040
- I mean we did funerals.
- Okay.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.020
Oh.
- We did weddings

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.700
and, but weirdly the
repertoire was very similar.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.938
I don't know why, we basically just sang

00:00:26.938 --> 00:00:29.310
like Christian hymns, old fashioned hymns

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.270
and we'd stand there like this
in these long velvet skirts

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.580
and it just, it's just so awesome

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.977
and so I just really
liked being a part of it.

00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:37.130
- Yeah.
- And then I did

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.700
school musicals as well.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.533
- Me too.

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:40.770
- Yeah, because it was like--
- We would have been friends,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:41.860
I mean, we can still be friends,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.540
but I just meant we would
have in high school.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.450
- Yeah, I think so.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.248
- Yes, we did all the same things.

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:47.470
- Who did she play?

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:48.970
I heard that you did Grease.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:49.870
- Okay, I did,

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.150
yeah I did Grease
- Yeah.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.770
- and Fiddler on the Roof in high school.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:53.610
- Yeah.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.080
- I was never cast in the lead role ever.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.410
So for kids out there watching,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.540
don't worry if the
teachers don't choose you,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.900
you could still
- You can still make it.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.890
- star in the most successful

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.690
musical comedy franchise of all time,

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.610
like you still could.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.060
- This, I am the light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.590
- So I, in Grease, I
was never cast is one,

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.667
I wanted to be like Jan,
that one that she's like

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:15.970
♪ Brusha, brusha, brusha ♪

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.060
- Oh I wanted to be Rizzo.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.620
- Yeah, oh, that was a good role too.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.650
I just didn't even set
my sights that high.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.940
And then, and then, so I didn't get cast

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.290
'cause they said I was too young

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:29.430
only the girls in year 11
can, can be the lead roles,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.930
you have to be in the chorus.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.600
And so me and my friend
we'd sit there like this

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.380
watching all the main girls.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.690
So in Grease, we'd sit there

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:37.970
and we'd watch the main girls

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:38.803
and we'd be like,

00:01:38.803 --> 00:01:41.644
oh, imagine if like something
bad happened to them,

00:01:41.644 --> 00:01:44.200
like, then maybe we could go on

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.820
'cause we know the songs,
we could just go on.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.680
And then we're standing
backstage at rehearsals

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.780
and a big television monitor falls on us.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.200
Like literally falls on our head.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.207
Like it was really dangerous.

00:01:55.207 --> 00:01:56.350
- That's karma.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.660
- And then we never wished ill

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.070
upon another performer ever again.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.300
- Yeah, that is karma at its finest.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.715
- It was, yeah.

00:02:03.715 --> 00:02:05.600
And then Fiddler on the Roof,

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.940
that was my first taste of fame actually

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.290
because I fell from the roof.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:13.120
So in that photo you can see
I played the ghost character

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.470
called Fruma Sarah

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:15.900
there I am, and I was like this ghost

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.740
and I descended from the roof.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.520
It was a very big entrance that I

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.353
- Yeah.
- helped devise.

00:02:20.353 --> 00:02:21.186
- It's very Pink.

00:02:21.186 --> 00:02:22.830
- Yeah and I came down

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.392
and there was a technical difficulty

00:02:24.392 --> 00:02:27.390
because it was a high school
production, wasn't that safe.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.910
So, and I fell from the roof,

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.710
went splat onto the stage.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.150
Everyone thought I was dead,

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.610
I became a local celebrity because of it

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.810
(laughing)

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.915
and I still was back out
on stage the next night,

00:02:39.915 --> 00:02:41.610
rocking it out.
- Show must go on.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.443
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:42.443 --> 00:02:43.410
When I fell
- And so, yeah.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:47.050
- I sprained all of my
ribs and my, my wrists,

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.800
but luckily it was fine.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.653
- Wow, okay.
- Yeah.

